WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.516 --> 00:00:04.478
Alice was having trouble holding the wiggling baby.

2
00:00:04.898 --> 00:00:06.900
She was still only nine inches high.

3
00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:37.475
As quickly as she could, Alice carried the baby outside the Duchess' The baby grunted, and Alice examined

4
00:00:37.535 --> 00:00:38.195
it closely.

5
00:00:39.056 --> 00:00:42.999
With each passing moment, it looked more and more like a pig.

6
00:00:46.763 --> 00:00:50.146
don't know what I'll do with this creature when I get home," Alice said.

7
00:00:50.946 --> 00:00:52.668
The baby grunted loudly.

8
00:00:52.688 --> 00:00:56.031
This time there could be no mistake.

9
00:00:56.051 --> 00:00:59.254
"This is definitely a pig!"

10
00:00:59.714 --> 00:01:00.254
Alice said.

11
00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:07.782
She put the animal on the ground, and it ran into the woods.

12
00:01:11.323 --> 00:01:13.344
Relieved, Alice started walking.

13
00:01:19.826 --> 00:01:24.408
She was soon startled to see the Cheshire Cat, sitting in a tree and grinning.

14
00:01:25.809 --> 00:01:29.890
Alice thought he looked friendly despite his long claws and sharp teeth.

15
00:01:31.471 --> 00:01:33.352
She decided to ask a question.

16
00:01:34.388 --> 00:01:38.072
"Cheshire Cat," Alice began, and the cat's grin grew wider.

17
00:01:38.092 --> 00:01:41.735
"Would you please tell me which way to go from here?"

18
00:01:43.577 --> 00:01:48.001
"That depends on where you want to go," the Cheshire Cat replied.

19
00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:51.364
Alice thought for a moment.

20
00:01:51.384 --> 00:01:54.387
"I don't really care as long as I get somewhere."

21
00:01:54.407 --> 00:01:59.872
"Then it doesn't matter where you go," the Cheshire Cat said.

22
00:02:01.452 --> 00:02:05.373
"You're sure to get somewhere if you walk far enough."

23
00:02:07.254 --> 00:02:10.875
While that answer was true, Alice didn't think it was helpful.

24
00:02:12.395 --> 00:02:13.895
She tried another question.

25
00:02:13.915 --> 00:02:16.336
"What sort of people live around here?"

26
00:02:17.676 --> 00:02:23.558
The Cheshire Cat waved his right front paw and said, "The Hatter lives in that direction."

27
00:02:24.938 --> 00:02:30.200
Pointing his left front paw, he said, "The March Hare lives over there.

28
00:02:31.616 --> 00:02:35.477
Visit whichever you like—they're both mad."

29
00:02:35.497 --> 00:02:43.439
"Mad?" "Yes, they're both quite insane.

30
00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:50.501
Then again, everyone here is mad, even you."

31
00:02:52.702 --> 00:02:54.082
Alice was curious.

32
00:02:54.102 --> 00:02:56.903
"How do you know that I'm mad?"

33
00:02:56.923 --> 00:03:01.609
"You must be, or you wouldn't be here.

34
00:03:06.473 --> 00:03:10.575
By the way, are you playing croquet with the Queen today?"

35
00:03:12.197 --> 00:03:14.498
Alice clapped her hands with delight.

36
00:03:14.518 --> 00:03:18.641
"I'd like that very much, but I haven't been invited yet."

37
00:03:23.985 --> 00:03:28.428
if you go, you'll see me there," the Cheshire Cat said.

38
00:03:29.556 --> 00:03:32.478
And then he vanished without another word.

39
00:03:33.599 --> 00:03:37.602
Alice wasn't surprised by this because she was getting used to odd things.

40
00:03:38.823 --> 00:03:43.526
While she was staring at the spot where the cat had been, he suddenly reappeared.

41
00:03:43.546 --> 00:03:48.710
"I forgot to ask what happened to the baby," he said.

42
00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:54.734
"The baby turned into a pig," Alice said calmly, as if that happened every day.

43
00:03:54.754 --> 00:04:00.713
"I thought it would," the Cheshire Cat said, and vanished again.

44
00:04:00.733 --> 00:04:06.216
"I'd better wait to be sure he isn't coming back," Alice said to herself.

45
00:04:08.016 --> 00:04:09.997
But the Cheshire Cat didn't reappear.

46
00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:17.400
After a few minutes, Alice walked toward the March Hare's house.

47
00:04:22.162 --> 00:04:25.424
seen hatters before, but I've never met a March Hare."

48
00:04:27.196 --> 00:04:28.997
As Alice said this, she looked up.

49
00:04:30.198 --> 00:04:32.679
There was the Cheshire Cat, sitting in a tree.

50
00:04:32.699 --> 00:04:36.321
"Did you say, 'pig' or 'fig'?"

51
00:04:36.981 --> 00:04:38.262
the Cheshire Cat asked.

52
00:04:38.282 --> 00:04:40.764
"I said, 'pig.'

53
00:04:41.744 --> 00:04:44.426
I wish you wouldn't keep appearing and disappearing so suddenly.

54
00:04:45.286 --> 00:04:46.387
You're making me dizzy!"

55
00:04:46.407 --> 00:04:48.848
"All right."

56
00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:56.112
This time the Cheshire Cat vanished slowly, beginning with his tail and ending with his mouth.

57
00:04:57.216 --> 00:05:01.759
His grin remained long after the rest of him had disappeared.

58
00:05:01.779 --> 00:05:07.483
"I've seen a cat without a grin, but never a grin without a cat."

59
00:05:08.604 --> 00:05:10.525
Alice shook her head in disbelief.

60
00:05:10.545 --> 00:05:13.707
"That's the strangest thing I've ever seen!"

61
00:05:16.489 --> 00:05:20.292
Alice soon came to a house with chimneys shaped like ears.

62
00:05:21.092 --> 00:05:22.593
The roof was made of fur.

63
00:05:22.613 --> 00:05:26.516
"That must be the March Hare's house," she said.

64
00:05:27.432 --> 00:05:32.083
And because the house was bigger than she was, Alice wanted to grow.

65
00:05:33.506 --> 00:05:37.755
She nibbled at her mushroom until she was two feet high.
